course: dictionary
lesson: 8923
title: The sieve: holes that let things through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sieve is a kitchen tool with a fine net or many small holes. Small bits fall through the holes, and big bits stay behind. Sieve can also be a verb: to sieve means to put something through a sieve.
explain: «Sieve the flour into the bowl before you add the eggs.» The sentence tells you what to do with the flour, and you can picture the lumps staying in the sieve. Always try your meaning in the sentence: "put the flour through a sieve" fits, so that is the right meaning.
explain: Sieve is also used in a phrase: «A memory like a sieve» means you forget things easily. A sieve lets things slip through, and a memory like that lets facts slip away. The word is not about a real kitchen tool here.
fact: A sieve is a tool with a fine net or many small holes.
fact: Sieve can be a noun (a sieve) or a verb (to sieve): sieve, sieves, sieved, sieving.
fact: Sieving separates mixtures, such as sand from gravel, or peas from water.
fact: «The biggest whales» have baleen, rows of bristly plates in the mouth that sieve tiny krill and small fish out of the water.
fact: «A memory like a sieve» is a phrase that means you forget things easily.
exercise: «Sieve the flour into the bowl before you add the eggs.» What does sieve mean here? | *To put flour through a sieve to remove the lumps | To throw the flour away | To bake the flour in the oven | To mix flour with water until it is sticky
exercise: «Toothed whales hunt one animal at a time instead of sieving the sea.» What does sieving the sea mean? | Freezing the sea into ice | *Letting the water pass through a sieve-like filter to catch tiny animals | Painting the sea a new colour | Drinking all the water in the sea
exercise: Nadia says, «He has a memory like a sieve, so he must remember everything.» What is wrong with her idea? | *The phrase means he forgets things easily | Sieves are made of metal, so the phrase is about strength | Nothing is wrong, she is right | The phrase means he has a strong memory
test: «The leopard seal's back teeth lock together like a sieve to strain krill.» What does like a sieve mean here? | *Like a tool with small holes that lets small things through and keeps big things back | Like a bowl that holds hot soup | Like a loud, noisy bell | Like a seal swimming very fast
test: Which sentence uses sieve as a verb? | A memory like a sieve forgets things | *The cook sieved the flour before making the cake | The cook used a sieve to drain the pasta | The sieve has many small holes
exam: «Gummy sweets are made by squirting hot syrup into shapes, then the powder is sieved, dried and used again.» In this sentence, what does sieved mean? | Painted with colour | *Put through a sieve to separate the fine powder from lumps | Thrown into the bin | Eaten by children
